SnapRAID Daemon Windows Signature verification
==============================================

The SnapRAID Daemon Windows installer is digitally signed. 
To ensure the integrity of this software, you have two
options for verification. 

IMPORTANT: Always obtain the 'am_ca.crt' file and the 
SHA-256 checksums directly from the official website:
https://www.snapraid.it

OPTION 1: INSTALL THE ROOT CERTIFICATE

By installing the 'am_ca.crt' file, Windows will be 
able to automatically verify the digital signature of 
this and all future SnapRAID Daemon installers.

Steps:
1. Download 'am_ca.crt' from https://www.snapraid.it
2. Right-click 'am_ca.crt' and select "Install Certificate".
3. Select "Local Machine" and click Next (requires Admin).
4. Select "Place all certificates in the following store".
5. Click "Browse" and choose 
   "Trusted Root Certification Authorities".
6. Click OK, then Next, then Finish.
7. Accept the security confirmation.

Once installed, right-click the installer .exe, select 
Properties, and the "Digital Signatures" tab will show 
"This digital signature is OK."

---

OPTION 2: MANUAL SHA-256 HASH VERIFICATION
If you prefer not to install the certificate, you can 
manually verify that the file has not been tampered 
with by checking its hash against the official record.

Steps:
1. Obtain the official SHA-256 hash from https://www.snapraid.it
2. Open PowerShell on your computer.
3. Type the following command:
   Get-FileHash .\snapraid-daemon-*.exe
4. Compare the output to the official hash.

If the hashes match exactly, the file is authentic and 
safe to run, even if Windows displays an "Unknown 
Publisher" warning.
